---
// Hand-tuned inline SVG: the Debug Agent's runtime data-flow when Alertmanager
// fires — the deterministic pre-LLM stage, the ReAct loop + verification gate,
// the LLM egress (Anthropic via Cloudflare AI Gateway), the MCP server fleet and
// the observability/platform backends it reaches (Loki, Tempo, Prometheus,
// Grafana, K8s/Flux, NATS, GitHub), and the resolution/action ladder.
// Single source of truth — rendered on the /debug-agent hub and in Paper #3.
// Style matches the homepage platform SVG (src/pages/index.astro): static,
// light-theme palette with hardcoded hex (cloud=amber, data=teal, external=beige).
// Brand glyphs are verified marks from simple-icons (CC0); a few niche backends
// (FalkorDB, Loki, Tempo, code search) use hand-drawn category glyphs.
---
<div class="glass-card p-4 sm:p-6 overflow-x-auto">
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 770 800" role="img" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;display:block;" font-family="ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif">
<title>BlueRobin Debug Agent — alert-triggered root-cause-analysis flow</title>
<desc>When Alertmanager fires a webhook, the Debug Agent (a .NET service on the Hetzner cloud worker) de-duplicates it, runs a deterministic no-LLM stage (Personalized PageRank plus BARO change-point scoring) seeded by a FalkorDB StackGraph query and Qdrant hybrid recall, then enters a bounded ReAct loop: an LLM turn (Anthropic Claude, egressing through the Cloudflare AI Gateway to frontier providers) alternates with an externalized Verification-Gate FSM that governs termination. The loop calls tools through an MCP server fleet that fans out to the LGTM observability and platform backends — Loki logs, Tempo traces, Prometheus metrics, Grafana, Kubernetes and Flux state, NATS events, GitHub commits and code search. Tool evidence builds a hypothesis tree under a grounding-based confidence soft-cap, and a confidence-tiered action ladder resolves to a notification (ntfy), a GitHub issue, attached patches, or an auto-PR a human merges.</desc>
